{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BerezinianCrossTermParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.BerezinianCrossTermParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BerezinianSelfAdjointCrossTerm"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BerezinianCrossTermParity.barOdd_blocks_not_adjoint_scaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BerezinianCrossTermParity.barOdd_blocks_not_adjoint_scaled","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BerezinianCrossTermParity.lean#L87-L99","doc":"**The bar-odd carrier's blocks are genuinely non-adjoint (off 2-torsion).** If\n`B` is bar-even, `C` bar-odd, and yet `C = k·σB` were adjoint-scaled with `k`\nbar-even, then `2·C = 0`. So the realizable bar-odd carrier of\n`crossTerm_bar_odd_of_barEven_barOdd_blocks` evades the adjoint-scaled obstruction\n`crossTerm_bar_even_of_adjoint_scaled` exactly off 2-torsion — the two families are\ndisjoint outside the degenerate 2-torsion locus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BerezinianCrossTermParity.crossTerm_bar_odd_of_barEven_barOdd_blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BerezinianCrossTermParity.crossTerm_bar_odd_of_barEven_barOdd_blocks","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BerezinianCrossTermParity.lean#L75-L85","doc":"**The non-self-adjoint route is realizable — and it is the `g·γ` model.** A\nbar-even block `B` (`σB = B`) times a bar-odd block `C` (`σC = −C`), dressed by a\nbar-even `Dinv`, gives a genuinely bar-ODD cross-term: `σ t = −t`. The dressing\n`g = B·Dinv` is bar-even and the weight `γ = C` bar-odd — exactly the\n`OddDecayWeightParity` factorization, here *derived* as the generic bar-odd carrier\nfrom independent (non-adjoint) blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BerezinianCrossTermParity.selfadjoint_is_adjoint_scaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BerezinianCrossTermParity.selfadjoint_is_adjoint_scaled","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BerezinianCrossTermParity.lean#L66-L73","doc":"#4421's self-adjoint result is the `k = −1` instance of the scaled obstruction:\n`C = −σB = (−1)·σB`, and `−1` is bar-even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BerezinianCrossTermParity.crossTerm_bar_even_of_adjoint_scaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BerezinianCrossTermParity.crossTerm_bar_even_of_adjoint_scaled","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BerezinianCrossTermParity.lean#L52-L64","doc":"**The adjoint-scaled cross-term is bar-EVEN, for any bar-even scaling.** If the\nodd off-diagonal blocks are adjoint-scaled `C = k·σB` with `k` bar-even (`σk = k`)\nand the even inverse-block `Dinv` bar-even (`σ Dinv = Dinv`), then the cross-term\n`t = B·Dinv·C` satisfies `σ t = t` — bar-EVEN — for any ring involution `σ`. The\ngraded-self-adjoint case `C = −σB` of #4421 is the `k = −1` instance; this shows the\nobstruction is not special to that sign but holds across the whole bar-even-scaled\nfamily. ","signatureChunk":0}]}